.TH "PB-CONFIG-REPOSITORY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-repository - Connect custom Git repositories and manage machine credentials


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config repository [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect custom Git repositories and manage machine credentials

.PP
Connect a Git repository to your account, inspect registered repositories, and configure authentication separately on this machine. Connecting a repository does not select local files; define explicit machine path rules before enabling synchronization.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for repository


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-repository-connect(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-repository-credentials(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-repository-list(1)\fP
